Parent: #7648
Depends on detection: #7788
Depends on generated-member facts: #7790
Framework/project facts: #6822 / #4746
Object/MRO semantics: #6672 / #4818
Freshness/invalidation: #4241 / #7309
Role-conflict consumer: #2972
Acceptance manifest: #7430

## Objective

Compose current-generation static Moose inheritance and `Moose::Role` relationships over canonical project facts.

This is one relationship-fact PR. It owns framework inheritance/role composition, role-provided/required method relations, conflict/order evidence, and reverse invalidation. It does not change live provider output or implement the Moose MOP.

## Supported first slice

Model reviewed static forms for:

```perl
extends 'Parent';
with 'Role::One', 'Role::Two';
```

under exact current Moose/Moose::Role activation and module/project identity.

Emit canonical facts for:

- child/consumer package identity;
- parent package and inheritance edge;
- consumed role package and composition edge;
- declaration source/generator anchor and argument ranges;
- composition order/index;
- role-provided and role-required source-backed method relationships where current facts exist;
- inherited/role generated members from #7790;
- explicit child/consumer method precedence;
- deterministic conflict/ambiguity disposition;
- framework/adapter/version, source/project generation, confidence, completeness, limitations, and reverse dependencies.

## Resolution and source tiers

Compose only current resolved package/module facts:

- workspace source;
- admitted #7470 external-dependency source;
- missing, ambiguous, generated-no-source, ambient, stale, or dynamic boundary.

Matching package text in another root or an unadmitted ambient installation cannot participate. External read-only source may support lookup but does not become editable refactor authority.

## Role and MRO boundary

- route inheritance and method availability through #6672's canonical object/MRO authority;
- preserve Moose-specific composition order/conflict semantics to the strength established for the selected version profile;
- do not flatten role composition into ordinary inheritance when the distinction affects method/conflict behavior;
- duplicate roles, cycles, aliases/exclusions, method modifiers, runtime role application, and metaclass mutation remain explicit boundaries unless the exact form is separately admitted;
- missing/dynamic role source does not invent provided methods;
- same-named methods in unrelated packages/roles are not conflicts without composition identity.

## Invalidation

Invalidate affected facts and dependents on:

- `extends`/`with` add/remove/reorder/rename;
- parent/role source edit/delete/re-add;
- provided/required/explicit method changes;
- generated attribute/member changes;
- Moose/framework version or activation change;
- module/root/environment/configuration change;
- close/reopen/root removal.

Stale composition work publishes nothing, and one unrelated project edit does not rebuild every adapter relationship.

## Fixtures

- single and multi-level static `extends`;
- one and multiple `with` roles;
- role consuming another role where the first slice can prove it;
- role-provided and required methods;
- parent and role generated members;
- explicit child/consumer override;
- same method from multiple roles;
- duplicate role and composition cycle;
- missing/ambiguous/dynamic parent or role;
- alias/exclusion/modifier form as admitted or explicit boundary;
- workspace and external-dependency parent/role source;
- same-name package/role in another root;
- edit/reorder/delete/re-add and stale publication;
- batch/live ProjectModel equivalence.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Static `extends` produces current canonical inheritance edges for the admitted profile.
- [ ] Static `with` produces current role composition and source-backed provided/required method relations.
- [ ] Parent/role generated members retain real source/generator anchors and producer identity.
- [ ] Explicit child/consumer methods retain deterministic precedence; role conflicts/order remain inspectable.
- [ ] Missing, ambiguous, cyclic, duplicate, dynamic, unsupported, generated-no-source, stale, and cross-root states remain explicit boundaries.
- [ ] Workspace and external-dependency source tiers remain distinct.
- [ ] Parent/role/member/activation edits invalidate dependent facts before reuse without unrelated project churn.
- [ ] #2972 can consume these canonical role relations rather than a parallel Moose role graph.
- [ ] No live provider behavior or refactor authorization changes in this PR.

## Non-goals

- No full Moose MOP, runtime role application, or metaclass execution.
- No broad `handles`, method modifier, alias, or exclusion semantics beyond separately admitted forms.
- No provider completion/navigation cutover.
- No generated-member rename or safe delete.
